          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9f7ab2302e67977d4ce464a5baccd49fd4f340499f23228ae417937ae4d62fab:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://infrastructure-as-code/komodo/stacks.toml#L57-L79",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4c4dc6ea956d9b93b0c0b04484d933145917fdc156acfa8b559f70a428b38121:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_66b43d908a114b8182d13efa9604b629",
      "statement": "There is no cross-project `depends_on` between the local stacks (deliberate since feature 020), so `auth` must be brought up before `mcm`'s `app` profile manually. The failure mode is not a crash or a hang: mc-service binds and serves immediately while running OIDC discovery in a background task, so with Keycloak unreachable `/health` answers while every protected request is rejected with 401 — a working-looking backend that refuses every login.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/mc-service/tests/integration/health_test.rs#L421-L455",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ff0dc32d44156c1236e3de5b042f12a9580ec39037720cb76d24092d0b26aaae:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://infrastructure-as-code/docker/stacks/auth.compose.yaml#L11-L12",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:40c4872fc98edd4dd4ec40093fa7fecb8b6307fbcf0813cefba7aa6ebe2b8aa4:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://infrastructure-as-code/docker/stacks/mcm.compose.yaml#L3-L5",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fd77a88dd800877fd67cd45fd0877ebfe18fce1c8cf8f4e16b7e9f70a15fd789:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a46b84c13f524277936ddedb83eefacf",
      "statement": "A Compose profile is not isolation from interpolation: Compose interpolates every service in an included file at parse time regardless of selected profiles, so a `${REGISTRY_HOST:?}` inside a profile-gated service made `up` fail for the entire `mcm` stack — including CI's app-e2e bring-up, which sets no `REGISTRY_HOST`. That is why the feature-073 backup destinations live in a separate compose file brought up explicitly instead of as another `mcm` profile.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://infrastructure-as-code/docker/backups/compose.yaml#L9-L16",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5b6109dcd2ab75f94fb629115ebbf1074227f78ab395b735cd06f6bc3b12c5ea:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://infrastructure-as-code/docker/stacks/mcm.compose.yaml#L15-L23",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5a67a2963fda7eb865b166f98e76de1b9785de685ccabfa16e4422fb0a55bbaa:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_287def3729684aed802ff68851f9cabe",
      "statement": "Adding a `${VAR:?…}` to a prod compose changes that stack's required inputs, and the only place they are declared is `stacks.toml`; `scripts/__tests__/komodo-stack-env.guard.test.mjs` enforces the coupling by asserting every required variable in a stack's prod compose files is supplied by that stack's `environment` block or its `additional_env_files`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
